## CLI read freshness

Freshness fields describe read responses only. Before acting on a CLI read,
check `stale` in `--json` output. If it is true with
`stale_reason: "sync_lock_busy"`, retry the same read after the current owner
finishes. Successful mutation acknowledgements omit these fields. A busy-lock
completion notice says when a write succeeded: never repeat a successful write.
Text mode prints a possibly stale read notice on stderr. See the sync skill for
response shapes and safe recovery; never delete the sync lock file to force
freshness.

## Creating work

`mtix create --type` accepts bug, feature, task, chore, refactor, test or doc (omitted = unset), independently of depth-derived hierarchy; `--assign <agent>` claims atomically as `in_progress`, overrides parent auto-claim and preserves the creator as author. MCP/REST/gRPC use `issue_type` and `assignee`. `mtix update --type` changes work classification (empty clears, omitted preserves). `mtix list --type` filters hierarchy; `mtix list --issue-type` filters work classification. See the planning skill for the full routine.

Project prefixes for local create (CLI, REST, gRPC and MCP) and `mtix init` must match `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9-]{0,19}$`: 1–20 uppercase letters, digits or hyphens, starting with a letter. An underscore or other invalid character returns `INVALID_INPUT` (gRPC: `InvalidArgument`) before a node or sequence is written.
A child also requires a valid prefix in its parent’s ID; choose a valid-prefix parent when a historical ID contains an underscore.


